  lead: "Grief is not a problem to be solved. It's the shape love takes when the person you love is gone. If it has knocked the wind out of you, that isn't weakness. That's the size of what you lost."
lead:
  - "There is no schedule for this. No tidy set of stages you move through and graduate from, no morning you wake up finished. Grief comes in waves, and the waves do not check your calendar. They can arrive at a wedding, in a grocery aisle, on an ordinary Tuesday that had no business being hard."
